const title = "Frigidaire Ice Maker Not Working? Causes & Fix — Same Day";
const description = "Frigidaire refrigerator not making ice? Start with the water filter, supply, and freezer temp. Why 'water dispenses but no ice' points to the ice-side valve.";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Why is my Frigidaire refrigerator not making ice?",
    a: "Work the water path first. The most common operator-fixable causes are a clogged water filter (replace every six months — low flow means little or no ice), a water supply valve that's partly closed or a kinked line behind the fridge, a frozen fill tube, a freezer that's too warm to cycle the maker, and the ice maker simply switched off or its feeler arm stuck up. If all of that checks out, the failed parts are usually the water inlet valve or the ice maker module. A useful Frigidaire tell: if water dispenses fine but there's no ice, the inlet valve has two separate solenoids and the ice side has failed while the dispenser side still works — that's a tech fix."
  },
  {
    q: "My Frigidaire dispenses water but won't make ice — why?",
    a: "That points straight at the ice side of the water inlet valve. Frigidaire uses a dual-solenoid valve: one solenoid feeds the door dispenser, the other feeds the ice maker, and they fail independently. So water flowing to the dispenser tells you the supply and filter are fine, but the ice-maker solenoid isn't opening to fill the mold. First rule out a frozen fill tube (thaw it gently) and a warm freezer; if those are clear, the ice-side solenoid needs testing and replacement, which is a tech job — the valve is electrically live and plumbed in."
  },
  {
    q: "How do I reset a Frigidaire ice maker?",
    a: "Start with the feeler (shut-off) arm: make sure it's down in the ON position, since a raised arm stops production. Then power-cycle the refrigerator — unplug it for a minute and restore power — which clears many transient ice-maker faults. Confirm the freezer is cold enough (around 0°F) and give it several hours to make the first batch. If the maker still won't cycle after that, the module or the inlet valve is the likely fault. Frigidaire doesn't publish a button-combo reset, so ignore online guides that claim a secret code."
  },
  {
    q: "Is my Frigidaire ice bucket part of a recall?",
    a: "It may be — worth checking, because it's a safety issue. Frigidaire's parent, Electrolux, has issued recalls where the plastic ice-level arm or the slim ice bucket can break into pieces that end up in the ice, a choking and laceration hazard. A 2022 recall covered roughly 370,000 units for a breaking ice-level arm, and a February 2024 recall covered about 400,000 side-by-side refrigerators (sold from late 2015 to 2019) with slim ice buckets that can crack. Look up your model on the official Electrolux recall site — if it's covered, the replacement part is free. See the safety section on this page for the link."
  },
  {
    q: "Is it worth repairing a Frigidaire ice maker that won't work?",
    a: "Usually yes. Most no-ice fixes are affordable — a filter, a fill-tube thaw, or the water inlet valve — against a refrigerator you're keeping. The ice maker module is a modest part too. Our techs verify the water path first (filter, supply, fill tube, temperature) so you're not paying to replace a valve when a clogged filter was starving the maker of water. In LA's hard water, mineral scale on the inlet-valve screen and fill tube is a common flow restriction, and clearing it is often the whole fix. $89 residential diagnostic, waived with the repair."
  }
];

